schema: encyclopedia-entry
object:
  title: Your First 90 Days Running a Local Node
  type: encyclopedia-entry
  page_type: guide
  summary: >-
    A paced playbook for standing up a ReFi local node without burnout:
    convene before you build (days 1-30), distribute the work early (days
    31-60), and only fund the thing once there's a track record (days
    61-90). Draws on ReFi Medellín's founding story (Tereza Bízková) and
    Commons Social Change Library burnout research, and points to existing
    networks (ReFi DAO, Greenpill Network, Regen Coordination) so organizers
    don't have to invent the whole stack.
  audience: people starting a new place-based ReFi/regenerative-finance node
  known_tensions:
    - >-
      grant-payout-timing-vs-early-costs — Gitcoin-style grants can take up to
      three months to pay out, so early events must be funded some other way
  related_concepts:
    - local-node
    - quadratic-funding
  related_resources:
    - refi-dao-local-node-incubator
    - glo-dollar
  maturity: raw
  ai_assisted: true
  provenance:
    origin: src/content/docs/first-90-days.md
    transformation: summarized
    authorship: ai-assisted
